700          /* The SOME/IP-SD protocol supports two option runs. Runs meaning that two different starting indices with differing
   701          length can be provided. Of course, this only works if the indices in both runs are consecutive.
   702
   703                  So, indices like this would work:
   704                          1 2 3 ; 7 8
   705
   706                  What wouldn't work is this:
   707                          1 2 3 ; 7 9
   708                          1 3 ; 7 8
   709          */
